Key Takeaways — Day 2
SQLAlchemy translates Python to SQL — I write Python, it writes the SQL

Models = Database Tables — One Python class per table

Sessions = Conversations — Open, use, close

create_all() auto-creates tables — No manual SQL needed

PostgreSQL users need permissions — Use GRANT to give access

Always activate venv — Packages only exist inside the virtual environment

pgAdmin Query Tool is useful for running raw SQL when needed

